#: ../../source/libraries/robot/loader.md:1
msgid "Loader Functions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/robot/loader.md:3
msgid ""
"These factory functions are the primary entry point for creating robot "
"worlds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/robot/loader.md:5
msgid ""
"`load(config=\"basic\", robot=\"standard\", *, position=None, "
"**overrides)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/robot/loader.md:7
msgid ""
"The simplest way to create a world and its robot in one call. Returns "
"`(world, robot)`. The robot is placed at `position` if given, otherwise "
"at the world's configured `start_position` (falling back to `(0, 0)`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/robot/loader.md:22
msgid "Worlds can also be loaded from JSON URLs, including GitHub `blob` links:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/robot/loader.md:32
msgid "`task(name, robot=\"standard\", *, position=None, debug=False)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/robot/loader.md:34
msgid ""
"Convenience wrapper around `load` for built-in lesson tasks. Returns "
"`(world, robot)`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/robot/loader.md:37
msgid "`load_world(config=\"basic\", **overrides)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/robot/loader.md:39
msgid ""
"Create a `RobotWorld` from a named built-in config or a `WorldConfig` "
"instance. Objects listed in the config are placed automatically. No robot"
" is created."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/robot/loader.md:49
msgid "`load_robot(config=\"standard\", world=None, *, position=(0, 0))`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/robot/loader.md:51
msgid ""
"Create a `Robot` and place it on the given world. If `world` is `None`, a"
" basic world is created automatically."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/robot/loader.md:61
msgid "`Loader` class"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/robot/loader.md:63
msgid ""
"`Loader` is a convenience class that bundles the factory functions as "
"static methods. Useful if you want to pass the factory as an object."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/robot/loader.md:66
msgid "API Reference"
msgstr ""

